      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is temporarily closed for skiing today, with increasing southwesterly winds forcing the mountain to shut down for the day. There's been 3 cm of new snow in the past 24 hours, holding the natural base at 112 cm; it's currently -1°C with winds around 29 km/h gusting to 50 km/h, easing slightly tomorrow before building again through the week. No lifts and runs are open today. The resort plans to try again tomorrow; the access road is chain-free but chains must be carried, with an active road hazard advisory in place. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 0 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
