      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, running a classic blustery spring day with a real mixed bag of conditions. There's been 3 cm of new snow in the past 24 hours, with the natural base holding at 150 cm at the top of Home Basin; it's currently 1°C with strong southwesterlies swinging northwest and easing through the afternoon, gusting to 32 km/h. A firm start after an overnight freeze is expected to soften quickly as the freezing level rises, with a few scattered snow showers down to 500m clearing this morning. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and the Beginner Platter are all running, all 3 of 3 lifts open, with 8 of 9 terrain zones open including Home Basin, Powder Bowl, Matukituki Basin, Saddle Basin, Summit Slopes and the terrain park; only Motatapu Chutes is on hold. Wind may interrupt lift operations at times through the day. (Issued: 1:37pm, 20 Sep) Backcountry and skinning access are both open; increased hazard is possible around Saddle access later as the freezing level rises, and the final Ride Tribe event of the season is on today. The access road is chain-free but chains must always be carried, with an active road hazard advisory and a free shuttle running from the bottom of the access road. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
